452,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":6.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.20359262949171986,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.016770456098547326,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":71.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01193,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"PennyMac Mortgage Investment Trust, through its subsidiary, primarily invests in residential mortgage-related assets in the United States. The company operates through: Credit Sensitive Strategies, Interest Rate Sensitive Strategies, and Correspondent Production segments. The Credit Sensitive Strategies segment invests in credit risk transfer (CRT) agreements and subordinate and credit-linked mortgage-backed securities (MBS). The Interest Rate Sensitive Strategies segment engages in investing in mortgage servicing rights, agency and senior non-agency MBS, and collateralized mortgage obligations (CMOs), as well as interest rate hedging activities. The Correspondent Production segment is involved in purchasing, pooling, and reselling newly originated prime credit quality loans directly or in the form of MBS. The company primarily sells its loans to government-sponsored enterprises. It has elected to be taxed as a real estate investment trust (REIT). It is not subject to U.S. federal income tax on the REIT taxable income it distributes to its shareholders. PennyMac Mortgage Investment Trust was incorporated in 2009 and is headquartered in Westlake Village, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David A. Spector | Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 62","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["PennyMac Mortgage Investment Tr is a small-cap real estate business with a $685M market cap.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Accruals are elevated at +34.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 20.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +34.4% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 58/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 55% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(PMT) Price Dynamics and Execution-Aware Positioning","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/149/PMT_Price_Dynamics_and_Execution-Aware_Positioning_110626120402_1793984642.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793984642.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.908,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Gregory L. Hendry Executes Automatic Sale of 2,443 PMT Shares at $7.73 on November 2, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/gregory-l-hendry-executes-automatic-sale-of-2443-pmt-shares-at-773-on-november-2-2026","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793856817.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Caesium Upgrade: Why Does It Matter for PMET Resources' (ASX:PMT) Quebec Project?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/lithium/caesium-upgrade-why-does-i